hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7601","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Harun bin Sulaiman told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, and Ahmad bin Ja’far told us Al-Qutay’i, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Imran Abi Al-Hakam Al-Sulami, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: Quraysh said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Pray for us that he make Safa for us. Gold and we believe in you. He said: “Will you do that?” They said: Yes. So he called, and Gabriel, peace be upon him, came to him and said: God, Blessed and Most High, recites his greetings to you and says: If you wish, turn Safa into gold. He disbelieved after that. I tortured him with a punishment that I do not punish anyone in the world, and if you wish, you can open for them the door of repentance and mercy. He said: “Rather, the door to repentance and mercy.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7601 - True"
"7602","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Muhammad Al-Farwi told us, Kathir bin Zaid told us, Al-Harith bin Abi Yazid narrated to us, saying: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Indeed, “A person’s happiness is to have a long life and God will grant him repentance.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7602 - True"
"7603","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah informed, Hisham bin Al-Ghaz, on the authority of Hibban ibn Abi al-Nadr, that he narrated to him, saying: I heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa’ saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “God, Blessed and Most High, said: I am when My servant thinks of me, so let him think of me whatever he wants.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7603 - Sahih and according to the conditions of Muslim"
"7604","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz Al-Baghawi told us, Abu Muslim told us, they said: Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Wasi’, on the authority of Shutair bin Nahar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Having good faith in God Almighty is part of the worship of God.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7604 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7605","Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i told us about Mecca, which God Almighty protected. Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us. Abdullah bin The reciter adds, on the authority of Hammam bin Yahya, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Ma’rour bin Suwayd, that Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, said: Al-Sadiq narrated to us Al-Masduq, may God bless him and grant him peace, in what was narrated on the authority of his Lord, Blessed and Most High, that He said: “A good deed is rewarded ten times its value or more, and an evil deed is One or I will forgive them. And if you were to meet Me with sins nearly as close to the earth as long as you did not associate Me with Me, I would meet you nearly as great as it, forgiving. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7605 - True"
"7606","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Firas al-Makki, the jurist, informed us of Mecca, which God Almighty has guarded. Yazid bin Abd al-Samad al-Dimashqi told us, Abu Mushahir Abd al-Ala bin Mushahar, Sa`id bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Idris al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abu Dharr May God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of God, Blessed and Most High, that he said: “O My servants, it is you who make mistakes. Night and day, and I am the one who forgives sins and I do not care, so ask forgiveness from Me and I will forgive you. O My servants, all of you are hungry except those whom I have fed. So seek food from Me and I will feed you, O My servants. All of you are naked except those whom I have clothed, so seek clothing from Me and I will clothe you. O My servants, if only the first of you and the last of you And the humans of you and the jinn of you were as pious as the heart of the most pious man among you. That would not increase My kingdom anything. O My servants, if only the first of you and the last of you and the human of you And your jinn were as ungrateful as the most wicked heart of any man among you. That would not diminish anything from My kingdom. O My servants, if only the first of you and the last of you, the human of you and the jinn of you... They gathered in one place and asked of Me, and I gave each one of them what he asked. This did not diminish My kingdom in the slightest, just as a sea is diminished when it is immersed. In it is a single dip. O My servants, it is only your deeds that I will preserve over you. So whoever finds good, let him praise God Almighty, and whoever finds other than “He does not blame anyone but himself.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7606 - It is in Muslim"
"7607","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Bishr bin Matar told me, Khalid bin Khadash Al-Zahrani told us, Bashar told us Ibn Al-Hakam, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, that Abu Dhar Al-Ghaffari urinated while standing, and some of his urine dripped onto the His legs and feet, and a man said to him: Some of your urine got on your feet and legs, but he did not answer him anything until he ended up at a people’s house. So he asked them to purify themselves, so they went out to him. He performed ablution and washed his legs and feet, then he went to the man and said: What did you say? He said: But now you have done so. Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, said: “This is the cure for this, and the cure for sins is to ask God Almighty for forgiveness.” Although this is authentic, its chain of transmission is authentic, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Abu Dharr, and this is its location.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7607 - True"
"7608","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz informed us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah told us, Yazid bin Harun informed us, Hammam bin Yahya, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, said: He was a storyteller in Medina called: Abdul Rahman bin Abi Amra, so I heard him. He says: I heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “A servant committed a sin and said: Oh My Lord, I have committed a sin, so forgive me. So his Lord said to him: My servant knew that he had a Lord who forgives sins and takes responsibility for them, so He forgave him. Then he remained for as long as God willing, then he committed another sin and said: O Lord, I have committed a sin, so forgive me. Then his Lord Almighty said: My servant knows that he has a Lord who forgives. I have forgiven my servant, so let him do what he wants. Then he sinned again and said: My Lord, forgive me my sin. So he said: God. Blessed and Most High: My servant committed a sin and learned that he has a Lord who forgives the sin and punishes the sin. Do whatever you wish, I have forgiven you. “This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7608 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7609","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abu Amr Ahmad bin Al-Mubarak told us, Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Jabir bin Marzuq Al-Makki told us, On the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah bin Omar bin Al-Khattab, on the authority of Abu Tuwala, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever commits a sin and knows that he has a Lord, if He wills, He will forgive him. He will forgive him, if He wills.” “He tortured him. It was God’s duty to forgive him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7609 - No, by God, who is Jabir to be a proof? Rather, he is indefinite and his hadith is objectionable, and Al-Amri is Al-Zahid and one of the trustworthy ones."
"7610","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told me, Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Al-Nadr bin Shumail bin Kharsha bin Yazid, told us Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, that he heard him say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man travels in the land of Tanufah and goes under a tree while his camel has his provisions and food on it, then he wakes up and his camel has actually escaped. He rose high and saw nothing. Then he rose high and saw nothing. Then he turned around and behold, he was with her dragging her reins. He was not more happy with her than with God. By the repentance of his servant when he turns to him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and he did not narrate it. “And it is witnessed by the hadith of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib, may God be pleased with it.” About them\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7610 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7611","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Ali al-Shaybani informed us, in Kufa, Ahmad ibn Qani` ibn Abi Ezra told us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, and Abu Naim, they said: Ubayd Allah bin Iyad bin Laqit told us, Iyad told us, on the authority of Al-Bara bin Azib, may God be pleased with them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “How can you say of the joy of a man whose camel has broken free, dragging its reins in a barren land that has no food or drink, and on which he has food and drink? So he searched for it until it was too difficult for him, then it passed around a tree and he hung on its reins and found it hanging on it? We said: Severe, O Messenger of God. He said: “By God, God is more happy with the repentance of His servant than a man is with his camel.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7611 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7612","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Shayban Al-Ramli told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim Al-Jazari, on the authority of Ziyad bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, said: My father and I entered upon Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, and he said to him My father: Did you hear the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Regret is repentance?” He said: Yes, I heard him say: “Regret is repentance.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7612 - True"
"7613","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, he said: I heard from Abdul Karim Al-Jazari says: We informed him of Ziyad bin Abi Maryam - he said: Sa’id bin Jubayr was not ashamed to narrate a hadith while I was sitting with Ziyad. He says, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, he said: I entered with my father to Abdullah, and my father said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Regret is repentance.” He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Regret is repentance.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They narrated it with this wording, but they agreed on the hadith of fik, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Aisha, may God be pleased with her: “If If you are innocent, God will absolve you, but if you are guilty of a sin, ask God for forgiveness and repent to Him, for if a servant confesses his sin and then repents May God accept his repentance.”"
"7614","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, and Abu Al-Hasan Al-Anzi told us, they said: We told us: Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Othman bin Saleh Al-Sahmi told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Ayyub, on the authority of Humaid Al-Taweel, he said: I said to Anas bin Malik: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Regret is repentance.” He said: Yes, and this is a hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not He brings him out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7614 - This is one of the evils of Yahya bin Ayyub"
"7615","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Anas bin Iyadh told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, Abdullah bin Dinar told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose After stoning Al-Aslami, he said: “Avoid this filth that God has forbidden. Whoever suffers, let him cover himself with God’s cover and repent until “By God, whoever whose page We change, We will impose upon him the Book of God Almighty.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7615 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7616","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Harmala bin Imran Al-Tajibi told us, that Abu Al-Sumait Saeed bin Abi Saeed Al-Mahri told him about His father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that Muadh bin Jabal wanted to travel and said: O Messenger of God, advise me. He said: “Worship God and do not associate anything with Him.” He said: O Messenger of God, increase me. He said: “If you do evil, do well.” He said: O Messenger of God, increase me. He said: “Be upright and improve your character.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7616 - True"
"7617","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub, Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Ziyad bin Al-Hubab told us, Ali bin Masada Al-Bahili told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Every human being is a sinner, and the best of sinners are “The ones who repent.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7617 - Ali bin Masada Lane"
"7618","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Dawud bin Sulaiman Al-Zahid told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid Al-Razi told us, Muhammad bin Issa told us, Salamah bin Al-Fadl, Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to me, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, Amr bin Al-Aas narrated to me, may God be pleased with him. On their authority, he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Every son of Adam will come on the Day of Resurrection having committed a sin, except that of Yahya.” Ibn Zakariya” said: Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, lowered his hand to the ground and took a small stick and then said: “That is because there was no He has what men have except the like of this oud, and for that God called him a master, a protector, and a prophet from among the righteous.” This is an authentic hadith according to Muslim’s conditions. And they did not bring it out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7618 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7619","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Qais bin Makhramah, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ali, on the authority of his grandfather Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “I did not worry about what the people of pre-Islamic times thought about except twice in the past, both of which God will protect me from.” Come from them. One night I said to a young man who was with me from the Quraysh in the upper part of Mecca, where the sheep of its people were grazing: “Give me a look at my sheep, so that I may spend the night in Mecca as they did.” The young man smiled and said: Yes, so I went out, and when I came to the nearest house in Mecca, I heard singing and the sound of tambourines and pipes, so I said: What is this? They said: So-and-so married so-and-so to a man from Quraysh who married a woman. So I was mesmerized by that singing and voice until my eyes fell asleep and I fell asleep. He woke me up until it touched the sun, so I came back and heard something like that, and I was told the same as what was told me, so I was distracted by what I heard, and my eyes were overcome by me, and nothing woke me up except He touched the sun, then I returned to my friend and he said: What did you do? So I said: I did not do anything.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By God, after that, I never cared about anything bad about what the people of pre-Islamic times did.” “Until God Almighty honored me with His prophecy.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7619 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7620","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Zakaria bin Ishaq told us, Amr told us Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, in the words of God Almighty: {Those who avoid the great sins. And immoral acts, except minor ones.} [An-Najm: 32] He said: “He is a man who commits an immoral act, becomes aware of it, and then repents from it.” He said: “He says:\n[The sea of rage]\nIf You forgive, O God, You will forgive greatly...and any servant of Yours who does not suffer.”\nThis is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7620 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7621","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abu Amer Abd Al-Malik bin Amr Al-Aqdi told us, Abd told us Al-Hamid bin Abdullah bin Katheer Al-Makki, Saeed bin Mina told us, saying: I was with Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, and I said: O Abu Huraira {Those who avoid major sins and immoralities except small ones} [An-Najm: 32] So what are small ones? He said: “Everything as long as the product does not enter the kohl pot, and if it does, then that is adultery.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7621 - True"
"7622","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me that a cyclist, He narrated it on the authority of Ibn Hujayr, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “If only you did not make mistakes. “God will bring a people who sin and forgive them.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “And the hadith of Abdullah bin Amr witnesses it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7622 - True"
"7623","Abu Amr Othman bin Abdullah bin Al-Sammak told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Abbad told us, Yahya bin Abbad, and Yahya bin Kathir told us Bin Dirham, they said: Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Balah Yahya bin Abi Sulaym, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with him. On their authority, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the servants had not sinned, God Almighty would have created people who would sin and then forgive them.” And He is the Forgiving, the Merciful.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7623 - Narrated by a witness"
"7624","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq, and Muhammad bin Ghalib narrated to us, saying: Abu Hammam Muhammad bin Mujib told us, narrated to us Ibrahim bin Tahman, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Al-Ma’rour bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, who said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “God Almighty says: Son of Adam, if you come a hand’s breadth closer to me, I will come a cubit’s length closer to you, and if you come a cubit’s cubit nearer to me, A large part of you, son of Adam, if you tell yourself a good deed and do not do it, I record it as one good deed for you, and if you do it, I record it for you ten times, and if you intend “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7624 - True"
"7625","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim, Al-Adl told us, Ubayy told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, On the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever remembers God Almighty in Himself, God Almighty remembers Him in Himself, and whoever mentions God in an assembly, God will remember him in an assembly greater than the assembly in which He mentioned him. And the best, and whoever draws near to God by a span, God will draw near to him an arm’s length, and whoever draws near to God a cubit, God will draw near to him by an arm. “Whoever comes to God trotting, God comes to him running.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it in this context, and Abu Abd The Most Gracious, this is: Abdullah bin Habib Al-Sulami.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7625 - True"
"7626","Abu Al-Hussein Ahmad bin Ishaq, Al-Adl Al-Saidalani, told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Sha’arani told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “You will enter Paradise except one who refuses and strays against God like the straying of a camel.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it. Narrated by Al-Bukhari, may God have mercy on him, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Awfi, on the authority of Fulayh bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Hilal bin Ali, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “All of my nation will enter Paradise except those who refuse.” It was said: O Messenger God and who refuses? He said: “Whoever disobeys me has refused.” The first text was narrated on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7626 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7627","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Asbagh bin Al-Faraj told us, Ibn Wahb told me, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Ali bin Khalid, he said: Abu Umamah Al-Bahili passed by Khalid bin Yazid bin Muawiyah, and asked him On the authority of Aline, a word he heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “All of you will enter Paradise.” Except for him who strays from God as a camel strays from its family.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7627 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7628","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Dawud told us Ibn Abi Hind, Abu Uthman Al-Nahdi told us, on the authority of Salman Al-Farisi, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God created On the day He created the heavens and the earth a hundred mercies, every mercy filling what is between the heavens and the earth, and He distributed of them as mercy among the creatures, with compassion therein. A mother cares for her child, and by her animals and birds drink water, and by her creatures have compassion, so when the Day of Resurrection comes, she will be restricted to The righteous, and He increased them by ninety-nine. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it in this context. Rather, they agreed on the hadith of Solomon. Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Suleiman, briefly, like the hadith of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Hurairah.”"
"7629","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl told us, and Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, they said: Bakkar bin Muhammad Al-Sirini told us, Awf bin Abu Jamila, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God has a hundred Mercy, He divided mercy among the people of the world and extended it to their own time, and He delayed ninety-nine mercies for His friends, and indeed, God Almighty He will take that mercy which He has apportioned among the people of this world up to ninety-nine, and He will complete it with a hundred mercies for His friends on the Day of Resurrection.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.”"
"7630","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told me, Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Wasiti and Muhammad bin Rumh Al-Samak told us, they said: Yazid told us Bin Harun, Saeed bin Iyas Al-Jariri reported, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Hairi, Jundub narrated to us, he said: A Bedouin came and geared up his saddle, then He unhitched it and prayed behind the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. When he greeted the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he came to his camel, unhitched it, then mounted it. Then he called out: O God, have mercy on me and Muhammad and do not associate in our mercy with anyone. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do you say he is more astray or his camel?” Did you hear what he said? They said: Yes. He said: “Indeed, God’s mercy is immense and vast. Indeed, God created one hundred mercies and sent down a mercy by which He shows compassion to creatures, both jinn and humans and their animals. “And with Him are ninety-nine mercies.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7630 - True"
"7631","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub bin Yunus Al-Shaybani told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Abdul-Malik bin Ibrahim told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Have mercy “Whoever is on earth will have mercy on you, whoever is in heaven will have mercy on you.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7631 - True"
"7632","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim, Al-Adl told me, my father told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Jarir told me, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of my father. Othman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: My close friend and guardian, the owner of this room, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Mercy is not withdrawn except “From a wretched man.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. This Abu Uthman is the freed slave of al-Mughirah and not al-Nahdi, even if he was al-Nahdi. “I ruled it to be authentic based on the conditions of the two Sheikhs.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7632 - True"
"7633","Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Darimi told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Omar bin Hafs Al-Shaybani told us, my father told us, Abd al-Rahim bin Kardam bin Artabaq bin Ghanam bin Aoun, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God has not created anything but that He created for it that which overcomes it, and He created His mercy that overcomes His wrath.” This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it like this.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7633 - This is objectionable"
"7634","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Hamdawayh, Al-Hafiz, informed us. Abu Ali Al-Hafiz informed us. Ali informed us. Ibn al-Abbas al-Bajli told us, Yahya bin Hakim told us, Khaled bin al-Harith told us, Shu’bah told us, Adi bin Thabit and Ata’ bin al-Sa’ib told me, On the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both - Shu’bah said: He mentioned one of them - on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “ Gabriel, peace be upon him, started putting clay in Pharaoh’s mouth for fear that he would say: There is no god but God, so that God Almighty may have mercy on him. “This is an authentic hadith.” The chain of transmission, but they did not narrate it.” There is evidence for it from the hadith of Ali bin Zayd.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7634 - True"
"7635","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Yusuf ibn Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that Gabriel, peace be upon him, said to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: If “You saw me taking some of the sea and putting it in Pharaoh’s mouth.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7635 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7636","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Zur’ah Al-Dimashqi told us, Ahmad bin Khaled Al-Wahbi told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Abdul-Wahid bin Hamza bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr told me, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her. On her authority, she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying in one of his prayers: “O God, give me a simple reckoning.” When he left, I said: O Messenger God, what is the easy reckoning? He said: “He looks at his book and ignores it. Indeed, O Aisha, whoever’s account is discussed, O Aisha, on that day will perish, and everything that befalls a believer is blasphemy.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it in this context.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7636 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7637","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abdullah bin Saleh Al-Muqri told us, Sulayman bin Harim Al-Qurashi told us, Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Suleiman Ibn Haram, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came out to us and said: “ My friend Gabriel came out from me just now and said: O Muhammad, by the One who sent you with the truth, God has five hundred of His servants, the servant of God Almighty. A year on top of a mountain in the sea, its width and length being thirty cubits by thirty cubits, and the sea surrounding it is four thousand parasangs on all sides. And God Almighty brought out for it a fresh spring the width of a finger, flowing with fresh water and soaking at the foot of the mountain, and a pomegranate tree gushing out He has a pomegranate every night, and it nourishes him for the day. When evening comes, he performs ablution, takes that pomegranate, eats it, and then stands for his prayer.So he asked his Lord, the Almighty and Majestic, at the time of the appointed time to hold him prostrate and not to make a way for the earth or for anything to spoil it until He resurrected him while he was prostrating. He said: So he did so. We will pass by him when we land, and when we ascend, we will find him in the knowledge that he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection. Then he will stand before God Almighty, and the Lord will say to him: Admit my servant into Paradise by my mercy. He will say: Lord, but because of my work. Then the Lord will say: Enter my servant. Paradise is by my mercy. He will say: O Lord, but by my deeds. The Lord will say: Admit my servant to Paradise by my mercy. He will say: O Lord, but by my deeds, so God will say. God Almighty says to the angels: Compare My servant with My blessings upon him and with his deeds, and you will find that the blessing of sight has encompassed the worship of five hundred years. And the blessing of the body remained as a blessing for him, and He would say: Enter my servant into Hell. He said: Then he would be dragged to Hell and call out: My Lord, by Your mercy, admit me to Paradise. So he says: Return him, and he stops in front of him and says: O my servant, who created you when you were nothing? He says: You, O Lord. He says: Was that by you or by my mercy? He says: Rather, by your mercy. He says: Who has empowered you to worship Him for five hundred years? And he says: You, O Lord,He will say: Who placed you on a mountain in the middle of the depths and brought out for you fresh water from salt water and brought out for you every night a pomegranate? You go out once a year, and you asked me to make you prostrate, so I did that to you? So he says: You, O Lord. Then God Almighty said: It is by My mercy and by My mercy that I admit you to Paradise. Admit my servant into Paradise. So the servant was blessed. You were, O my servant, and God will admit him to Paradise. Gabriel, peace be upon him, said: “Things are only by the mercy of God Almighty, O Muhammad.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission, for Suleiman bin Haram Al-Abid is one of the ascetics of the people of the Levant, and Al-Layth bin Saad does not narrate on the authority of unknown people.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7637 - No, by God, and Suleiman bin Haram is not supported"
"7638","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn Sulayman al-Zahid told us, Al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn al-Layth told us, Ahmad ibn Shurayh told us, Muhammad informed us Ibn Yunus Al-Yamimi, Yahya Ibn Shu’bah Ibn Yazid told us, Ishaq Ibn Abdullah Ibn Abi Talha Al-Ansari told me, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever says: There is no god but God will enter Paradise and it is obligatory for him.” Paradise, and whoever says: Glory be to God and praise be to Him a hundred, God will record for him a thousand good deeds and twenty-four good deeds. They said: O Messenger of God, then no One of us will perish. He said: “Indeed, one of you does good deeds that were to be placed on a mountain weighing heavy, then blessings come and you take away those, then the Lord relents afterward.” That is by His mercy.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration that bears witness to the hadith of Sulaiman bin Haram, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7638 - True"
"7639","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari informed us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Maryam informed us. Al-Ghasani, on the authority of Damra ibn Habib, on the authority of Shaddad ibn Aws, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A wise man is He subjugated himself and worked for what is after death, and the helpless one is he who follows his own desires and hopes against God Almighty. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7639 - True"
"7640","Ahmad bin Kamil bin Khalaf Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Saad Al-Awfi told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz bin Omar bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf, and Abdul Rahman bin Humaid bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of Amer bin Saad, on the authority of his father, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The believer is an unbeliever.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7640 - True"
"7641","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Dhuli told us, Musaddad told us, Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Al-Hakam, narrating on the authority of Al-Gharif, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of the Faithful Spirit He said: He said: “The Lord Almighty said: The servant’s good deeds and his bad deeds will be given, and he will interchange some of them with the other. If there remain good deeds, God will expand for him in “Paradise” He said: So I went to Yazdad and he told us a similar hadith. I said to him: So if the good deed goes away? He said: {Those are those from whom We accept the best of what they have done} [Al-Ahqaf: 16] - and he read to his saying - {They are promised} [Al-Ahqaf: 16] I said to him: So I saw God Almighty said: “So no soul knows what has been hidden from them of comfort” [Al-Sajdah: 17] He stated: “The servant does secret work, his reward is with God Almighty and Majestic.” But the people did not know about it, so God made secret for him on the Day of Resurrection the comfort of an eye.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration for the Yemenis, but they did not narrate it, and the ruling that Narrated by Al-Mu`tamir bin Suleiman. He is: Al-Hakam bin Aban Al-Adni, and Al-Gharaif is: Abu Harun Al-Gharaif bin Ubaid Allah \"Yamani\"\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7641 - True"
"7642","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrafi told us that what I mentioned was true, in Marwa, Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Fadl Al-Balkhi narrated to us, Hafs bin Omar Al-Adni, Al-Hakam bin Aban told us, Abu Harun Al-Gharaif bin Ubaid Allah told me that Abu Al-Sha’atha’ told him that Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, narrated to him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to him that the Faithful Spirit narrated to him: “Indeed, God Almighty has decreed that On the Day of Resurrection, the servant’s deeds will be presented with his good deeds and his bad deeds, and he will recount some of them with the other. If only one good deed remains for him, God will expand for it. In Paradise whatever he wants.” Al-Hakam bin Aban said: So I went to Abu Salama, Yazid, and said to him: So if the good deed is gone and nothing remains? Then He said: {Those are those from whom We accept the best of what they have done} [Al-Ahqaf: 16] - to His saying - {Those they were promised} [Al-Ahqaf: 16]"
"7643","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari told us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Some people wish they had done more evil.” They said: Why, O Messenger of God? He said: “Those whose evil deeds God has changed into good deeds.” This Abu Al-Anbas is Sa’id bin Kathir, and its chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7643 - True"
"7644","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Bishr bin Matar told us, Ubaid Allah bin Omar Al-Qawariri told us, Harami bin Amara bin Abi told us Hafsa, Shaddad bin Saeed Abu Talha Al-Rasibi narrated to us, on the authority of Ghailan bin Jarir, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Some people from my nation will come with sins like mountains, and God will forgive them and place them on “The Jews and Christians.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “It was narrated by Al-Hajjaj bin Nusayr, on the authority of Abu Talha, with additions in Its text\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7644 - Shaddad bin Saeed Al-Rasibi has many evil deeds"
"7645","It was narrated to me by Ali bin Hamshadh, Abu Muslim narrated to us, and Muhammad bin Ghalib narrated to us, saying: Hajjaj bin Nusayr narrated to us, Shaddad bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ghaylan Ibn Jarir, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “This nation will be gathered in three groups. Types: A type will enter Paradise without reckoning, a type will be given an easy reckoning, and a type will come upon their backs like well-mounted mountains. Then He asks God about them, and He knows best about them. He says: Who are they? They say: These are servants of yours. So He says: Take it away from them. And bestow it on the Jews and Christians, and admit them into Paradise with my mercy.”"
"7646","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya Al-Qurashi told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Sabah, Muhammad bin Sulaiman told us, Hisham bin Ziyad told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God does not teach any servant to regret a sin except that He forgives him before asking him for forgiveness for it.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7646 - Rather, Hisham bin Ziyad is abandoned"
"7647","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Al-Khidr bin Aban Al-Hashimi told us, Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, in His Almighty saying: {Perhaps they will return} [The Romans: 41] He said: “They repent.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7647 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7648","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya told us, Sulayman bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Hammam and Hammad bin Salamah told us, They said: Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha told us, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I struck someone. He said: He did not ask him about it, and the prayer was established, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. When he finished his prayer, he said: Oh Messenger of God, I have struck a punishment, so abide by the Book of God. He said: “Did you pray with us?” He said: Yes. He said: “You have been forgiven.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7648 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7649","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl bin Ghazwan told us, Sadaqah bin Al-Muthanna, Rabah bin Al-Harith narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Burdah, who said: While I was standing in the market in the emirate of Ziyad, I struck with one of my hands on the The other was astonishment, and a man from the Ansar whose father had been in the company of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What amazes you, O Abu? Purdah? I said: I am more astonished than a people whose religion is one, whose prophet is one, whose calling is one, whose Hajj is one, and whose campaign is one. It is permissible. Some of them killed others. He said: Do not be surprised, for I heard my father. He told me that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “My nation is a nation She is merciful. There is no reckoning or torment upon her in the Hereafter, but her torment is in killing, earthquakes, and temptations.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not “He brings him out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7649 - True"
"7650","Abu Al-Abbas told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Burdah, he said: I was With Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad, the heads of the Kharijites were brought. Whenever they passed by a head, he said: To Hell. So Abdullah ibn Yazid said to him: First. Do you know that I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The torment of this nation has been placed by its own hands in its world.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. The two sheikhs did not narrate it, but Muslim alone narrated the hadith of Talha bin Yahya, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa: “My nation is a merciful nation.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7650 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7651","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubaid bin Musa told us, Shayban bin Abdul Rahman told us, On the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Sa’d, Talha’s client, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: I have heard from The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said, “If I only heard him once or twice until he counted seven, but I heard him more than that,” he said: Al-Kafl was one of the children of Israel who did not hesitate to absolve himself of his sins. A woman came to him and he gave her sixty dinars on the condition that he would have intercourse with her. When He sat next to her as a man sits next to his wife. She trembled and cried, so he said: What makes you cry? Do you have to hate it? She said: No, but this is work that I have never done, but need forced me to do it. He said: So you are doing this and you have never done it before. “He said: “Then He came down and said: Go, and the dinars are yours. He said: Then he said: “By God, the kifl will never disobey his Lord.” He died that night and it became written on his door: “This kifl has been forgiven.” A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7651 - True"
"7652","Hamza bin Al-Abbas Al-Uqabi told us, Muhammad bin Isa bin Hayyan told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Sulayman, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, in the Almighty’s saying: {And she cared for him and they cared for her} [Yusuf: 24] He said: “A man sat by her as a man sits with his wife, and he was called: O son of Jacob, have you committed adultery and become like a bird whose feathers are plucked and flies but has no feathers? “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7652 - True"
"7653","Ali bin Abdullah Al-Hakimi told me, in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Khalaf bin Musa bin Khalaf told us, my father told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was exhorting his companions when three people passed by. Then one of them came and sat next to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the second went away for a while and then sat down, and the third went on his face, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: “As for this one who came and sat with us, he repented, so God turned to him, and as for the one who went away for a little while and then sat down, he was ashamed, so God was ashamed.” “And as for the one who passed away, he became self-sufficient, so God dispensed with him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7653 - True"
"7654","Abu Ja`far Abdullah bin Ibrahim Al-Qurashi told us, in Baghdad, Musa bin Al-Hasan bin Abbad told us, Muhammad bin Musab told us Al-Qarqasa’i, Salam bin Miskin, and Al-Mubarak bin Fadalah told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Sari’, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet was brought May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, a captive Bedouin, and he said: I repent to God Almighty, but I do not repent to Muhammad. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He knew the truth.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7654 - Ibn Mus’ab is weak"
"7655","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid Al-Bayruti told us, Muhammad bin Shuaib bin Shapur told us, Muhammad bin Abi Muslim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that a young man from among the immigrants He came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, ask forgiveness for me, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became distracted from him, so he repeated that to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, three times. Then when he saw that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not asking forgiveness for him, the boy in the hands of the Messenger of God said: May God bless him and grant him peace three times: O God, forgive me, O God, forgive me, O God, forgive me, for your Messenger did not ask forgiveness for me. When the boy left, Gabriel, peace be upon him, came down to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, would you please ask forgiveness for the boy, for God is He has forgiven him, so follow him until you know that God has forgiven him and say to him: He asks forgiveness for you. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came after him until he caught up with him. When he caught up with him, he said: “O boy, God Almighty has forgiven you.” So ask forgiveness for me.” The boy said: Oh God, I ask you for forgiveness for your Messenger, O God, I ask you for forgiveness for your Messenger and your Prophet just as you have forgiven me, for you are ample. Forgiveness, and You are the Most Merciful of those who show mercy"
"7656","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Wahb Al-Dimashqi told us, Muhammad bin Shuaib told us Ibn Sabour, Muhammad Ibn Abi Muslim told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ata Ibn Abi Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, so he mentioned the hadith. Likewise, “This is a strange hadith with a strange chain of transmission and text, and the narrators of this hadith on the authority of others are trustworthy, except that Muhammad bin Abi Muslim is unknown.” And God knows best.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7655 - Strange"
"7657","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Muhammad bin al-Jahm bin Harun al-Nimri told us, Abu Dawud told us, Sadaqah told us Ibn Musa, Muhammad Ibn Wasi’ told us, on the authority of Samir Ibn Nahar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “ Your Lord Almighty said: If My servants had obeyed Me, I would have given them rain to drink by night, and I would have made the sun shine on them by day, and I would not have heard them. \"the sound of thunder\"\nThe Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Having a good opinion of God is part of good worship.”\nThe Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Renew your faith.” It was said: O Messenger of God, how do we renew our faith? He said: “Say often, ‘There is no god but Allah.’ This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7657 - Charity is weak"
"7658","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Abdullah bin Salih told me, Al-Layth told me, on the authority of Yazid Ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Uqba ibn Amir, may God be pleased with him, that a man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Oh Messenger of God, one of us commits a sin. He said: “It will be written against him.” He said: Then he should ask forgiveness for it and repent? He said: “He will be forgiven and repented.” He said: Then he will sin again? He said: “It is prescribed for him, and God does not tire until you tire.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7658 - True"
"7659","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Omar bin Hafs Al-Sadusi told me, Asim bin Ali told us, Abd Al-Rahman bin Thabit bin Thawban, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God Almighty forgives His servant or accepts His servant’s repentance as long as he does not commit sin.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7659 - True"
"7660","Abu Al-Abbas Ahmad bin Harun Al-Faqih told us dictation, Bishr bin Musa bin Shaykh bin Umairah Al-Asadi told us, Abdullah bin Salih told us Ibn Muslim Al-Ijli, Abdul Rahman Ibn Thabit Ibn Thuban told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Omar Ibn Nu’aym, on the authority of Usama Ibn Salman: That Abu Dhar al-Ghifari, may God be pleased with him, told them that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God forgives His servant so long as he does not The veil falls.” It was said: O Messenger of God, what is the veil? He said: “That the soul dies as a polytheist.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7660 - True"
"7661","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani informed us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab informed us, Ja`far bin Aoun informed us, Hisham informed us Ibn Saad, Zayd Ibn Aslam narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn al-Bilamani, who said: I heard a man, one of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever repents to God the day before he dies, God will accept it from him.” He said: So I narrated that. Another man from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Did you hear that? I said: Yes, he said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever repents to God half a day before he dies, God will accept From him.” So I told that to another man, and he said: Did you hear that? I said: Yes, he said: So I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever repents to God before he dies, will accept his sacrifice.” From him. He said: I told that to another man from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Did you hear that? I said: Yes. He said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever repents to God before he gargles, God will accept from him.” This is how it was narrated by Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad Al-Darawardi, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam"
"7662","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mal informed us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told us, Ibrahim ibn Hamza told us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad told us, On the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Bilamani, on the authority of a man, one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard And he said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, there is no person who repents one day before he dies but God accepts his repentance.” So I told a man about that. From the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Hisham, whether"
"7663","So Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Khuzaymah ibn Qutaybah al-Kashshi told us, from the original of his book, Fulayh ibn Amr al-Kashshi told us, Al-Ma’mal ibn Ismail, Sufyan al-Thawri told us, he said: I wrote to Abd al-Rahman bin al-Bilamani, asking him about a hadith that he narrated on the authority of his father, so he wrote He told me that his father told him that he sat with a group of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and one of them said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whoever repents to God a year before his death, God will accept his repentance.” Another said to him: Did you hear it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes. He said: And I heard him. Another said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever repents to God Almighty before... He died in a month, may God accept his repentance.” Another said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes. He said: And I heard him. Another said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever repents to God Almighty before... His death on the day God turned to him in repentance.” Another said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes. He said: And I heard him. Another said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever repents to God Almighty before... He died an hour later, and God accepted his repentance. Another said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes. He said: And I heard him. Another said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever repents to God before the gargling will repent.” May God be upon him.” Sufyan bin Sa’eed, may God be pleased with him, even though he had a better memory than Al-Darawardi and Hisham bin Sa’d, he did not mention hearing him in This hadith is from Ibn al-Bilamani, nor from Zayd ibn Aslam. He was only mentioned in a citation and written form, so what is said about it is the statement of those who said on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ibn Al-Bilamani, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Abdullah bin Nafi’ Al-Madani was healed and explained in His narration on the authority of Hisham bin Saad that the companion Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them, and the authenticity of that \"\"\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7663 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7664","Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid ibn Ibrahim al-Asadi al-Hafiz narrated to us in Hamdan, Umair ibn Madras narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nafi’ narrated to us, Hisham bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Bilamani, who said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with him. About them he says: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever repents a year before his death, his repentance will be accepted,” until he said: “in a month,” until he said: “On a Friday,” until he said: “on a day,” until he said: “in an hour,” until he said: “with hiccups,” so I said: Glory be to God, did not God Almighty say: {And it is not Repentance is for those who do evil deeds, until when death approaches one of them, he says, “Indeed, I repent now” [An-Nisa: 18]? Abdullah said: I am only telling you about what I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7664 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7665","Amr ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Adl informed me, Al-Sari ibn Khuzaymah informed me, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti informed me, Ishaq ibn Yusuf, Al-Awwam bin Hawshab told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that He said: “The prescribed prayer until the prayer that follows it is an expiation for what is between them - he said: Then he said after that - except for three: associating partners with God, And he broke the deal and abandoned the Sunnah. “As for breaking the deal, you give the imam your pledge of allegiance to him, then you approach him and fight him with your sword.” “Leaving the group” is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7665 - True"
"7666","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told us, Abdullah bin Raja told us, Harb bin Shaddad told us, Yahya told us Ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdul Hamid Ibn Sinan, on the authority of Ubaid Ibn Umair, on the authority of his father, that he narrated to him and he had companions that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said in the Farewell Pilgrimage: “Indeed, the righteous friends of God are those who perform the five daily prayers that were prescribed for him, and fast Ramadan. He thinks that his fast is due, and he gives the zakat on his wealth as he expects it, and he avoids the sins that God has forbidden. Then he A man asked him and said: O Messenger of God, what are the major sins? He said: “They are nine: associating others with God, killing the soul of a believer unjustly, fleeing on the Day of Battle, consuming an orphan’s property, and consuming usury. And he slandered the chaste woman, disobedience to Muslim parents, and declaring the Sacred House lawful before you, whether alive or dead. Then he said: “He does not die.” A man who did not commit these major sins, perform prayer, or pay zakat, unless he was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a house whose doors were made of “Gold” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7666 - True"
"7667","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl informed us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Ja’far bin Aoun informed us, Al-Masoudi informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman, the client of the Talha family, on the authority of Issa bin Talha, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who referred it to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “No one who weeps out of fear of God Almighty will enter the fire until the milk returns to the udder, and no dust and smoke will gather in the path of God Almighty. Hell is in the nostrils of a Muslim ever.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7667 - True"
"7668","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marwa, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, Ibrahim bin Sulayman told us, Abu Ja`far al-Razi told us, on the authority of Rabi’ Ibn Anas, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever remembers God and his eyes overflow with fear of God Until his tears hit the earth, God Almighty will not punish him on the Day of Resurrection.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7668 - True"
"7669","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Yazid Ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Uqba ibn Amir Al-Juhani, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no The work of a day except that it is sealed from it, and not a night except that it is sealed from it, until when something comes between the servant and the work, the Keepers say: O our Lord. “This is the work of your servant before he was prevented from doing the work, and you know it best.”\nAmr said: Abdul Karim told me, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, may God be pleased with him: “Indeed The first to know of the death of the servant is the memorizer, because he is lagging behind in his work and his sustenance is lacking. If no sustenance comes out, he knows that he is dead.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7669 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7670","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi narrated to us, Bishr bin Omar Al-Zahrani narrated to us, Abdul Aziz bin Abi Salama, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, who said: Abdullah bin Abbas and Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with him, met On their authority, Ibn Abbas said to him: Which verse in the Book of God do you most hope for? He said: {Say: O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of God’s mercy} [Az-Zumar: 53] “And He said: “But what Abraham said when he said: {Have you not believed? He said, “Yes, but so that my heart may be at peace.” [Al-Baqarah: 260] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7670 - There is an interruption"
"7671","Ali bin Issa told me, Musaddad bin Qatan told me, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told me, Muawiyah bin Hisham told me, Sharik bin Abdullah told me, On the authority of Uthman bin Abi Zar’ah, on the authority of Abu Sadiq, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Paradise has eight gates, seven of which are closed and one door is open for repentance until the sun rises in its direction.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7671 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7672","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Mahran told me, my father told me, Amr ibn Sawad al-Sarhi told me, Ibn Wahb told me, Amr told me Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Darraj, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The devil He said: By Your Might, O Lord, I will never cease to mislead Your servants as long as their souls remain in their bodies. Then the Blessed and Most High Lord said: By My Might and Majesty, I will not “I will forgive them as long as they ask for My forgiveness.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7672 - True"
"7673","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani, Al-Hafiz, told us, Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Dahli, the martyr, told us. Abdul Rahman bin Al-Mubarak Al-Absi told us, Fudayl bin Sulaiman told us, Musa bin Uqba told us, Ubaid Allah bin Sulayman Al-Aghar told me, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Everything that the son of Adam speaks is written. Therefore, if he commits a serious sin and would like to repent to God Almighty, then let his companion come and extend his hands to God Almighty, then say: Oh God, I repent to You for it and never return to it, for he will be forgiven as long as he does not return to that action. “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7673 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7674","Al-Hasan bin Al-Halim Al-Maruzi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed us, Abdan informed us, Sulayman bin Al-Mughirah informed us, on the authority of Humaid Ibn Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Qatada, he said: Ubadah, meaning Ibn Qart, said: “You will do deeds today that are... More beautiful to your eyes than hair, if we were to consider it at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to be one of the calamities.” He said: So I said to Abu Qatada: So how? If only our time had reached this point? He said: “This is what I say.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7674 - True"
"7675","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Awf Al-Tai told us, Abu Al-Mughirah told us, Sa’id bin Sinan told us, Umm Al-Sha’a’a told me, On the authority of Umm Isma Al-Awsiah, who had met the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no A Muslim commits a sin unless the angel appointed to count his sins stops for three hours, and if he asks God for forgiveness for his sin in any of those He did not stop him for it and he will not be punished on the Day of Resurrection.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7675 - True"
"7676","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrifi told me about Marw, Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Fadl Al-Balkhi told us, Hafs bin Omar Al-Adni told us, Al-Hakam bin Aban, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Indeed, God is Blessed and Most High. He says: Whoever among you knows that I have the ability to forgive sins, I will forgive him, and I do not care as long as he does not associate anything with Me. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7676 - Al-Adani is wah"
"7677","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Safwan bin Salih told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Al-Hakam bin Musab told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdullah bin Abbas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Whoever seeks forgiveness frequently, God will make for him a relief from every worry and a way out from every distress, and He will provide for him from where he does not expect.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7677 - Al-Hakam bin Musab contains ignorance"
"7678","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told me about Al-Ray, Muhammad bin Al-Faraj Al-Azraq told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad Al-Masisi told us, Yunus told us Ibn Abi Ishaq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Juhayfah, on the authority of Ali Ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever commits a sin in this world and is punished for it, God is more just than to extend His punishment to His servant, and if he commits a sin in this world, he will cover it up.” God is upon him. God is too generous to go back on something that He has pardoned.” The Last Book of Repentance and Repentance.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7678 - Al-Dhahabi was silent about it here and came with the number 8165, and Al-Dhahabi said there: According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
